  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5486",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the relationship with VM-CUB-1 through a series of molecular pathways that involve the P2X purinoceptor 1 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. These intermediates are all targets of a common compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which suggests a shared mechanism of action. The evidence indicates that doxorubicin may act through a pathway that involves the activation of P2X purinoceptors or the modulation of lipid metabolism, leading to the targeting of VM-CUB-1. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the involvement of a common intermediate compound support the idea that VM-CUB-1 is a downstream effector in this pathway. The integration of these findings highlights a potential mechanism where doxorubicin influences cellular processes through a series of molecular interactions, ultimately affecting VM-CUB-1.",
